  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Toluene or substituted toluene is converted to benzylidene diacetate on treating with chromic oxide in acetic anhydride. The benzylidene diacetate can be hydrolysed to corresponding benzaldehyde with aqueous acid.</p><p>Chromyl chloride oxidises<br/>methyl group to a chromium complex, which on hydrolysis<br/>gives corresponding benzaldehyde. The reaction is known as Etard reaction.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2e946792-c97f-4635-9248-950de9c558f3.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 271px;\"/></p>",
